G0302.def:
ἄν, 
conditional particle, 
which cannot usually be separately translated in English, its force depending on the constructions which contain it (see further, LS, see word; WM, §xlii; M, Pr., 165 ff.; MM, VGT, see word). 
__1. In apodosis, 
__(i) with indic, imperfect or aor., expressing what would be or would have been if (εἰ with impf., aor. or plpf.) some condition were or had been fulfilled: Luc 7:39 17:6, Jean 5:46, Galates 1:10, Matthieu 12:7 24:43, 1 Corinthiens 2:8, Actes 18:14, 1 Jean 2:19, al. The protasis is sometimes understood (as also in cl.): Matthieu 25:27, Luc 19:23. In hypothetical sentences, expressing unreality, ἄν (as often in late writers, more rarely in cl.) is omitted: Jean 8:39 15:24 19:11, Romains 7:7, Galates 4:15; 
__(ii) with opt., inf., ptcp. (cl.; see LS, see word; M, Int., §275; M, Pr., 167:4). 
__2. In combination with conditional, relative, temporal, and final words; 
__(i) as in cl., with subj., 
__(a) in protasis with εἰ, in Attic contr. ἐάν, which see; 
__(b) in conditional, relative, and temporal clauses (coalescing with ὅτε, ἐπεί, etc.; see: ὅταν, ἐπάν, etc.), ever, soever; 
__(α) with pres., ἡνίκα, 2 Corinthiens 3:15; ὃς ἄν, Romains 9:15 (LXX) 16:2, al.; ὅσοι ἄν, Luc 9:5; ὡς ἄν, Romains 15:24 (M, Pr., 167); 
__(β) with aor., ὃς ἄν, Matthieu 5:21, 22, 31; ἕως ἄν, until, Matthieu 2:13, Marc 6:10, al.; ὡς ἄν, as soon as (M, Pr., 167), 1 Corinthiens 11:34, Philippiens 2:23. On the frequently use of ἐάν for ἄν with the foregoing words, see: ἐάν; 
__(ii) in late Gk., when some actual fact is spoken of, with indic.: ὅταν (which see); ὅπου ἄν, Marc 6:56 (M, Pr., 168); καθότι ἄν, Actes 2:45 4:35; ὡς ἄν, 1 Corinthiens 12:2. 
__3. in iterative construction, with imperfect and aor. indic. (M, Pr., 167): Actes 2:45 4:35, 1 Corinthiens 12:2. 
__4. with optative, giving a potential sense to a question or wish: Actes 8:31 26:29. 
__5. Elliptical constructions: εἰ μή τι ἄν (M, Pr., 169), 1 Corinthiens 7:5; ὡς ἄν, with inf., as it were (op. cit. 167), 2 Corinthiens 10:9.

G0331.def:
ἀνάθεμα, -τος, τό
(ἀνατίθημι), 
Hellenistic for Attic ἀνάθημα (Bl., § 27, 2); 
__1. prop. = τὸ ἀνατιθέμένον, that which is laid by to be kept, a votive offering (as ἀνάθημα in 2Ma.2:13, Luc 21:5—where LT read -θεμα, see M, Pr., 46). 
__2. [As equiv. in LXX for חֵרֶם,] devoted, a thing devoted to God (see Driver, De., 98 f., and cf. Lévitique 27:28-29), hence; 
__(a) of the sentence pronounced (Deutéronome 13:15), a curse: Actes 23:14; 
__(b) of the object on which the curse is laid, accursed (Deutéronome 7:26): Romains 9:3, 1 Corinthiens 12:3 16:22, Galates 1:8-9 (see ICC on Ro.; Lft., Ga., ll. with; Cremer, 547; Tr., Syn., § v; MM, VGT, see word).†

G0337.def:
ἀν-αιρέω, -ῶ 
[in LXX for הָרַג hi., מוּת hi., נָכָה hi., etc. ;] 
__1. to take up: mid., Actes 7:21. 
__2. to take away, make an end of, destroy (for late exx. of various senses, see MM, VGT, see word); 
__(a) of things (as frequently in cl. of laws, etc.): Hébreux 10:9; 
__(b) of persons, to kill: Matthieu 2:16, Luc 22:2 23:32, Actes 2:23 5:33, 36 7:28 9:23-24, 29 10:39 12:2 13:28 16:27 22:20 23:15, 21 23:27 25:3 26:10, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:8, WH, txt., R, txt.†

G0352.def:
άνα-κύπτω
[in LXX: Job 10:15 (נָשָׂא רֹאשׁ), Dan LXX, Su 1:35 * ;] 
to lift oneself up; 
__(a) bodily; Luc 13:11, Jean 8:7, 10; 
__(b) mentally, to be elated: Luc 21:28 (cf. MM, VGT, see word).†

G0386.def:
ἀνά-στασις, -εως, ή
(ἀνίστημι), [in LXX: Sophonie 3:8 (קוּם), La 3:63 (קִימָה), קִימָה), Psaumes 66:1-20 title., Dan LXX 11:20, 2Ma.7:14 2Mac 12:43 * ;] 
__1. a raising up, awakening, rising (in Inscr. of the erection of a monument, see MM, VGT, see word): Luc 2:34. 
__2. a rising from the dead (see DCG, ii, 605b); 
__(a) of Christ: Actes 1:22 2:31 4:33 Romains 6:5, Philippiens 3:10, 1 Pierre 3:21; ἐξ ἀ. νεκρῶν, Romains 1:4 (ICC, in l); ἐκ νεκρῶν, 1 Pierre 1:3; 
__(b) of persons in OT hist. (e.g. 3Ki.17:17 ff.): Hébreux 11:35; 
__(with) of the general resurrection: Matthieu 22:23, 28 22:30 Marc 12:18, 23 Luc 20:27, 33 20:36, Jean 11:24, Actes 17:18 23:8 24:15, 2 Timothée 2:18; ἀ. ἐκ νεκρῶν, Luc 20:35, Actes 4:2; τῶν νεκρῶν, Matthieu 22:31, Actes 17:32 23:6 24:21 26:23, 1 Corinthiens 15:12-13 15:21 15:42, Hébreux 6:2; ἀ. ζωῆς, resurrection to life (cf. 2Ma.7:14, ἀ. εἰς ζωήν) and ἀ. τ. κρίσεως, τ. to judgment, Jean 5:29; ἀ. τ. δικαίων, Luc 14:14; κρείττων ἀ., Hébreux 11:35; on ἡ ἀ. ἡ πρώτη, Apocalypse 20:5-8, see Swete, in l, Weste. on Jean 5:1-47, but see also Thayer, see word; by meton. of Christ as Author of ἀ., Jean 11:25 (see DB, iv, 231; Cremer, 307).†

G0387.def:
ἀνα-στατόω, ῶ
(ἀνάστατος, driven from home; ἀνίστημι), [in LXX: Daniel 7:23 (דּוּשׁ;* also in Aq., and in π. (see Deiss., LAE, 80 f.; MM, VGT, see word),] 
to stir up, excite, unsettle: with accusative; 
__(a) to tumult and sedition: Actes 17:6 21:38; 
__(b) by false teaching: Galates 5:12 (see Milligan, NTD, 73 f.).†
